WEBVTT

00:10.271 --> 00:13.056
These looks were easy to design

00:13.100 --> 00:15.058
once I found my inspiration,

00:15.102 --> 00:18.540
which is Central Park,
of course.

00:18.583 --> 00:22.761
And it didn't need to be
complicated.

00:22.805 --> 00:25.547
I said to the team,
"Let's make it chic,

00:25.590 --> 00:29.072
"let's make it expensive,

00:29.116 --> 00:31.988
and the clothes should feel like
a picnic in a Manet." You know?

00:32.032 --> 00:34.991
And who is this
interesting fellow?

00:35.035 --> 00:38.386
This is Mr. Spagooti.
He's a rock star.

00:38.429 --> 00:39.996
The kids love him
like a sex god.

00:42.085 --> 00:43.695
He's a traditional manga artist
from Tel Aviv

00:43.739 --> 00:45.132
collaborating on
our athletic wear line.

00:45.175 --> 00:48.004
We will incorporate his drawings

00:48.048 --> 00:50.702
throughout the collection
like this.

00:50.746 --> 00:53.183
With jacquard,

00:53.227 --> 00:55.707
along with the number five
at the back

00:55.751 --> 00:58.014
to commemorate our anniversary.

00:58.058 --> 01:00.930
Get this girl a cigarette.
She's freezing. Come on.

01:00.973 --> 01:02.888
Well, I've taken enough
of your time.

01:02.932 --> 01:05.065
I'll leave you to your work.

01:05.108 --> 01:07.328
It was great to see you again,
Chairman.

01:07.371 --> 01:10.505
Oh, just before I forget,
just one more thing.

01:10.548 --> 01:12.811
My grandson is a huge fan.

01:12.855 --> 01:16.032
I-I heard. I will
send him a signed sample

01:16.076 --> 01:17.294
as soon as they're in.

01:17.338 --> 01:19.601
He would be most grateful.

01:19.644 --> 01:22.169
They sell out too fast,
even for me.

01:23.170 --> 01:25.737
Eniola will send a package over.

01:27.652 --> 01:29.785
Okay. Fine.

01:46.932 --> 01:49.152
- Whoa!

01:50.675 --> 01:53.896
- Dope!

02:02.687 --> 02:05.081
You remember that
Tommy Hilfiger thing?

02:05.125 --> 02:06.561
Man, Tommy Hilfiger--

02:06.604 --> 02:08.171
Is Tommy Gear owned
by a white person?

02:08.215 --> 02:10.826
- It's got to be an Indian.
- He got to be Indian.

02:10.869 --> 02:12.784
Hey, yo, dude coming down the
steps look like Drop Dead Fred.

02:12.828 --> 02:13.959
- Good morning.
- Hey.
- Good morning.

02:14.003 --> 02:16.875
- Hi.
- Hi. Good morning.

02:16.919 --> 02:18.442
Oh.

02:18.486 --> 02:20.183
Thank you so much
for meeting us

02:20.227 --> 02:21.445
on such short notice.

02:21.489 --> 02:23.882
We are so happy to meet you.

02:23.926 --> 02:25.362
I am a little bit-- Look,

02:25.406 --> 02:27.190
can we get some food first?
'Cause all I had was

02:27.234 --> 02:29.366
that English breakfast,
and that did not hit,

02:29.410 --> 02:30.976
so I need a real meal.

02:31.020 --> 02:32.761
Yeah, anything you want.

02:32.804 --> 02:35.285
Um, let's place a food order
right now. Yeah.

02:35.329 --> 02:37.287
- All right, bet. You ready?
- Mm-hmm.

02:37.331 --> 02:40.377
Can I get smoked ribs
with a dry rub?

02:40.421 --> 02:43.685
And, um, let me get
a-a simple, God,

02:43.728 --> 02:46.601
a simple-ass mac and cheese,
please. Thank you.

02:46.644 --> 02:49.212
Certainly. And anything
for you, Earn?

02:49.256 --> 02:51.736
Oh, I'm good.

02:51.780 --> 02:54.913
Darius, you want anything?

02:54.957 --> 02:57.220
Yeah. Jollof rice.

02:57.264 --> 02:59.440
Jollof? I haven't heard of it.

02:59.483 --> 03:02.399
It's as if your taste buds
are being scammed

03:02.443 --> 03:05.185
by a Nigerian prince
at a Burna concert.

03:07.230 --> 03:09.711
- Okay.
- One of those, please.

03:09.754 --> 03:13.410
So, yes, uh, joll-of
for Darius.

03:13.454 --> 03:15.804
And now that lunch is settled,

03:15.847 --> 03:18.241
you've probably heard about
our little mix-up.

03:18.285 --> 03:21.984
- Yeah. Yeah.
- Yeah. Yeah...

03:22.027 --> 03:25.074
Look, we want to apologize
to the community properly

03:25.117 --> 03:26.771
with your help, you know.

03:28.077 --> 03:29.557
All right, what I got to do?

03:29.600 --> 03:32.734
So, nothing.
That's the beauty of it.

03:32.777 --> 03:35.867
There's a press event later
where we'd introduce you

03:35.911 --> 03:38.522
and the rest of our new
diversity advisory board

03:38.566 --> 03:42.657
to our partnership.
And Eniola will be your liaison.

03:42.700 --> 03:45.442
What's the financial aspect
to this?

03:45.486 --> 03:47.270
We can't give you actual cash

03:47.314 --> 03:48.750
'cause that would look
disingenuous.

03:48.793 --> 03:51.056
But, well, we-we can donate
to any charity

03:51.100 --> 03:52.797
or foundation of your choosing.

03:54.843 --> 03:56.627
All right. Okay.

03:56.671 --> 03:59.543
Uh, but I'm gonna need
a custom suit

03:59.587 --> 04:00.979
for the press event.

04:01.023 --> 04:03.286
A custom suit. Uh, yeah. Okay.

04:03.330 --> 04:04.766
- Yeah.
- Yeah. Okay.

04:04.809 --> 04:06.376
Three.

04:06.420 --> 04:09.336
Okay, yes. Three. Okay.

04:09.379 --> 04:10.728
I need a bunch of clothes, too.

04:10.772 --> 04:12.208
Free.

04:12.252 --> 04:14.558
- Uh, yeah. Okay.
- Fine.

04:14.602 --> 04:17.605
- Three years.
For three years.
- Whoa.

04:17.648 --> 04:20.129
Three? In the studio
we'll try on a lot of clothes.

04:20.172 --> 04:21.696
- A lot of clothes. Yeah. Mm-hmm.
- Yeah. Okay.

04:21.739 --> 04:23.088
- Okay. Okay.
- Free tailoring, too.

04:23.132 --> 04:25.134
Okay, easy.

04:25.177 --> 04:28.920
Uh, I'll send the tailor up,
and you can then... Okay?

04:28.964 --> 04:31.923
Gentlemen, it has been
such a pleasure.

04:31.967 --> 04:33.185
Thank you so much.

04:33.229 --> 04:34.709
Lovely to meet you.

04:34.752 --> 04:37.712
And anything in the showroom
is yours, okay?

04:37.755 --> 04:40.758
- Eh, even this?
- No, no. Except that.

04:40.802 --> 04:42.717
- What you mean, man? Come on.
- Okay. Bye-bye, bye-bye.

04:42.760 --> 04:44.371
It's, like, the most exclusive
thing you got.

04:48.375 --> 04:50.812
What's up?

04:50.855 --> 04:53.597
- We can talk later.
- No, nigga, say it now.

04:53.641 --> 04:56.383
Man, he don't even
speak English anyway.

04:58.210 --> 04:59.342
This feels like
an Uncle Tom photo op.

04:59.386 --> 05:01.039
Why are we doing this?

05:03.215 --> 05:05.522
Man, you know how hard it is

05:05.566 --> 05:07.307
for me to get, like,
designer shit free

05:07.350 --> 05:09.352
from my stylists, in Atlanta?

05:09.396 --> 05:11.963
This way I'm plugged in.

05:12.007 --> 05:14.226
Yeah, but you can
buy all that shit.

05:14.270 --> 05:16.011
I shouldn't have to, man.

05:16.054 --> 05:17.534
We work too damn hard.

05:17.578 --> 05:20.189
This way we get free gifts,
runway seats,

05:20.232 --> 05:21.843
free designer bags
for the thots, man.

05:21.886 --> 05:24.193
Shit, my drip gonna
completely change.

05:24.236 --> 05:26.195
You're not worried about,

05:26.238 --> 05:27.936
you know,
what the streets think?

05:27.979 --> 05:31.374
The streets?

05:31.418 --> 05:33.158
Man, fuck the streets.
Man, I've shot niggas.

05:33.202 --> 05:34.943
Finito. Should be two hours.

05:34.986 --> 05:37.337
All right. Gracias.

05:39.687 --> 05:41.906
Reputation.
You trying to tell me

05:41.950 --> 05:43.952
that you, uh, you wouldn't take
any of these

05:43.995 --> 05:45.562
free designer gifts?

05:45.606 --> 05:47.390
Free shoes?
You wouldn't do that?

05:47.434 --> 05:49.697
If it was me?

05:49.740 --> 05:53.353
Yeah, I might still
do it, but...

05:53.396 --> 05:55.006
I'd make sure they put me
on the board

05:55.050 --> 05:57.226
for at least five years so I
could learn the infrastructure.

05:57.269 --> 05:59.707
Then I'd start my own program.

05:59.750 --> 06:02.187
Like teach Black people
how to reinvest

06:02.231 --> 06:03.667
in their communities.

06:03.711 --> 06:06.017
Like help out Black
entrepreneurs

06:06.061 --> 06:07.497
and business owners.

06:07.541 --> 06:09.586
Like a "reinvest in your hood"
campaign.

06:09.630 --> 06:11.501
Something that might
actually help people.

06:11.545 --> 06:13.329
Ooh, Lord, man, I don't know
why I asked,

06:13.373 --> 06:14.939
'cause I knew you was
gonna be on that

06:14.983 --> 06:17.202
"spook sitting by the door,"
Martin Luther King,

06:17.246 --> 06:18.465
Ebeneezer Baptist Church shit.

06:18.508 --> 06:20.597
- Goddamn, man. Like...

06:20.641 --> 06:22.120
And you know what they do
to that dude every time.

06:22.164 --> 06:23.121
- Yeah.
- Say it with me.

06:23.165 --> 06:24.993
They kill him.

06:25.036 --> 06:26.298
Thank you, man.

06:26.342 --> 06:27.604
Try them shoes on.

06:30.781 --> 06:34.219
Hi. I'm Sharon,
head of hospitality.

06:34.263 --> 06:36.221
- Are you Darius?
- Yes.

06:36.265 --> 06:39.747
Hi. Um, I got an email request

06:39.790 --> 06:41.270
for jollof.

06:41.313 --> 06:43.054
- Yeah.
- It's so weird.

06:43.098 --> 06:45.187
My husband and I, we know every
Michelin place in town,

06:45.230 --> 06:46.754
but I don't know that.

06:46.797 --> 06:48.233
Is that--
It's Ghanaian, right?

06:48.277 --> 06:51.628
No, no.

06:51.672 --> 06:54.979
Who told you that?
Was it a Ghanaian?

06:55.023 --> 06:58.635
No. No.

06:58.679 --> 07:01.856
Um, it's just my mistake.

07:01.899 --> 07:05.468
Is there a particular place
that you go to?

07:05.512 --> 07:08.602
There is a place across town
that's supposed to be legendary.

07:08.645 --> 07:10.168
It's just too out
of the way, but...

07:10.212 --> 07:11.474
Oh, we can take you.

07:11.518 --> 07:14.521
- Yeah? Are you sure?
- Yeah.

07:14.564 --> 07:16.566
That's literally my job, babe.

07:16.610 --> 07:19.526
We'll gather up
all the gift bags,

07:19.569 --> 07:21.528
and I will call the car
around, yeah?

07:21.571 --> 07:22.877
- Let's do it.
- Great.

07:33.235 --> 07:34.889
- Hey, Sam.
- Hey, boo.

07:34.932 --> 07:36.847
Mwah. Ooh, cute.

07:36.891 --> 07:39.459
Thank you.

07:39.502 --> 07:42.331
Uh, how are you not freezing?
Where are your pants?

07:42.374 --> 07:44.420
Girl, I'm hot, if anything.

07:44.464 --> 07:46.291
Khalil, you're a damn liar.

07:46.335 --> 07:48.380
Beauty is pain.

07:50.731 --> 07:52.341
Demarco.

08:03.961 --> 08:05.310
That's Rose.

08:07.748 --> 08:10.185
Voice of an angel.

08:11.665 --> 08:15.930
Hi, I'm Khalil--
activist, writer, foodie.

08:15.973 --> 08:18.019
I know who you are, man.

08:18.062 --> 08:21.152
So, is this your first time
apologizing for white people?

08:21.196 --> 08:23.633
- Apologizing?
- Yeah. It's the best.

08:23.677 --> 08:25.809
The dinners are amazing.

08:25.853 --> 08:29.552
I haven't paid for a meal
in 73 police shootings.

08:29.596 --> 08:32.033
- Oh, I think we're on.

08:35.210 --> 08:36.646
I forgive you.

08:39.910 --> 08:41.956
This is probably some bullshit.

08:41.999 --> 08:45.350
I am the least prejudiced
person in this room,

08:45.394 --> 08:47.352
in the world, even.

08:47.396 --> 08:49.659
So what do I do now,

08:49.703 --> 08:51.879
just perform a couple of songs
or some shit?

08:51.922 --> 08:54.621
After Bouchet is done
apologizing,

08:54.664 --> 08:55.752
they'll open the floor
to questions.

08:55.796 --> 08:57.841
Just say they didn't mean it,

08:57.885 --> 08:58.886
smile and take these pictures.

08:58.929 --> 09:00.061
We need to reflect,

09:00.104 --> 09:02.106
- and we need to move on.

09:02.150 --> 09:04.152
Hey. Relax, sweetie.

09:04.195 --> 09:06.720
You got this.

09:06.763 --> 09:10.985
And we are investigating
ourselves internally.

09:11.028 --> 09:15.119
And now I proudly cede
to our panel of experts.

09:22.039 --> 09:24.781
Clermont with Le Parisien.

09:24.825 --> 09:28.785
Um, Paper Boi,
after this, is racism over?

09:31.919 --> 09:33.616
Um...

09:33.660 --> 09:35.705
- Fuck no. Obviously.

09:35.749 --> 09:37.577
- Oh, my God.

09:37.620 --> 09:39.970
I mean, look, la-- look
at the porn industry, right?

09:40.014 --> 09:41.929
- They be having bitches...
- I think what he means

09:41.972 --> 09:44.540
is that with our new initiative,

09:44.584 --> 09:48.196
we believe racism
will be done by 2024.

09:57.074 --> 09:58.946
Oh!

10:13.961 --> 10:16.920
This movie is so crazy.

10:16.964 --> 10:19.270
Yeah.

10:19.314 --> 10:20.445
Is it Hamlet?

10:20.489 --> 10:23.274
Not quite.

10:23.318 --> 10:25.059
It's called Sharon Stone.

10:25.102 --> 10:26.495
- It has a sequel.
- Ah.

10:28.889 --> 10:31.239
The atmosphere in this place
is so cool.

10:31.282 --> 10:32.849
- Oh?
- Yeah.

10:32.893 --> 10:34.851
- Welcome to Eko Chops.
- Hi.

10:34.895 --> 10:38.986
- Hey.
- I'm Mimi. Any drinks?

10:39.029 --> 10:40.727
Uh, water's fine.

10:40.770 --> 10:42.729
- Tap. Tap would be...
- Okay.

10:42.772 --> 10:44.774
I'll be right back
to explain the menu.

10:44.818 --> 10:46.602
- Okay.
- A-Actually, I know what I want.

10:46.646 --> 10:49.779
I'm just gonna do Moin-Moin
with the egg or some liver.

10:49.823 --> 10:52.695
Liver? Are you Naija?

10:52.739 --> 10:55.089
- Yes, I'm Naija.
- Ooh.

10:55.132 --> 10:58.745
Couldn't tell.
Your hair is so Igbo.

11:01.269 --> 11:02.705
River State. Ijaw.

11:04.054 --> 11:05.403
- Oh, yeah?
- Mm.

11:05.447 --> 11:07.449
- Rivers boy?
- Yeah.

11:07.492 --> 11:08.842
When was the last time you went?

11:10.582 --> 11:12.976
- Uh, don't do this to me.

11:13.020 --> 11:14.108
It's been too long.

11:15.544 --> 11:17.894
The Moin-Moin is plain.

11:17.938 --> 11:20.027
For next time, bring
your own meat or vegetable

11:20.070 --> 11:21.550
you want them to put in.

11:21.593 --> 11:23.552
The kitchen will cook
for you no problem.

11:23.595 --> 11:25.423
Um, thank you, Auntie.

11:25.467 --> 11:27.730
Oya, what you want to eat?

11:27.774 --> 11:28.905
Uh...

11:30.733 --> 11:33.083
Oh, I meant to ask you earlier,

11:33.127 --> 11:35.564
what does "Naija" mean?

11:35.607 --> 11:37.740
- Naija means Nigerian.
- Ah.

11:37.784 --> 11:39.829
Yeah, this is
a Nigerian restaurant,

11:39.873 --> 11:43.398
Nigerian food
and Nigerian music playing.

11:43.441 --> 11:45.705
I see.

11:45.748 --> 11:49.796
And apart from the goat,
this dish is exquisite.

11:49.839 --> 11:51.754
Is it just rice?

11:51.798 --> 11:54.714
- It's jollof. Naija jollof.
- Oh.

11:56.193 --> 11:59.283
And what, what's she eating?

11:59.327 --> 12:00.720
It's okra soup.

12:02.852 --> 12:05.246
Ugh, I love her.

12:05.289 --> 12:09.511
- Yeah, she's sweet.
- I need to get
her business card.

12:09.554 --> 12:11.382
There is a lot
of growth potential.

12:11.426 --> 12:13.080
Uh, my husband, he has
lots of commissary kitchens

12:13.123 --> 12:14.951
all over the city.

12:14.995 --> 12:18.128
It's all about good PR.

12:18.172 --> 12:20.391
Cool.

12:20.435 --> 12:21.871
Yes, mainly
fish and chip trucks,

12:21.915 --> 12:25.614
but he's moving
into brick and mortar.

12:25.657 --> 12:28.095
I'm actually joining him
full-time.

12:28.138 --> 12:32.316
I feel like boneless fish
is an abomination.

12:32.360 --> 12:34.405
Oh, God, I know. I hate fish.

12:34.449 --> 12:36.407
I mean, I like fish,
but boneless fish is...

12:36.451 --> 12:38.279
Is your Shazam working?

12:38.322 --> 12:39.976
Mine's not working.

12:48.463 --> 12:50.160
Homestretch.
Hope you're all rested.

12:50.204 --> 12:51.422
Um, I'll be here to take notes
for the committee.

12:51.466 --> 12:54.208
Alfred, why don't you go first?

12:54.251 --> 12:55.644
What do you want
out of this meeting?

12:59.866 --> 13:03.434
Shit, all right, okay. Uh...

13:03.478 --> 13:05.045
You know, I'm--
This is something

13:05.088 --> 13:06.220
I've been thinking about
for a long time, right?

13:06.263 --> 13:08.352
So, you know,

13:08.396 --> 13:11.051
obviously, everybody at this
table has the opportunity

13:11.094 --> 13:13.140
- to help Black people.
- Right. Mm-hmm, mm-hmm.

13:16.447 --> 13:18.145
Go on.

13:18.188 --> 13:20.669
Yeah, so, um...

13:20.712 --> 13:23.193
I was thinking
that we could do, like, a...

13:23.237 --> 13:25.674
- like a capsule collection.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

13:25.717 --> 13:27.458
Yeah, a-and a campaign.

13:27.502 --> 13:30.679
A campaign to, um,
teach Black people

13:30.722 --> 13:33.029
how to reinvest
back into their communities.

13:33.073 --> 13:34.161
- Hmm.

13:34.204 --> 13:36.467
- Cool.
- Yeah.

13:36.511 --> 13:39.470
- Oh.
- Demarco, what do you want?

13:39.514 --> 13:40.863
Uh, yeah, yeah.

13:40.907 --> 13:44.258
Yeah, I-I want the new
Off-White Nikes. Signed.

13:44.301 --> 13:48.044
And a round trip to Mauritius,
business class.

13:48.088 --> 13:50.264
- Mm-hmm.
- Business class, though.

13:50.307 --> 13:51.656
- Mm-hmm.
- Sam?

13:51.700 --> 13:53.615
I want 1,000 copies of my book

13:53.658 --> 13:55.269
to be purchased
for sensitivity training.

13:58.925 --> 14:00.709
She'll work on that.

14:00.752 --> 14:02.885
I wish for ten tickets
to Raisin in the Sun,

14:02.929 --> 14:04.278
for my charity,

14:04.321 --> 14:05.888
and Julia Roberts
better be in it,

14:05.932 --> 14:07.716
not an understudy
like last time.

14:07.759 --> 14:09.022
- Mm-hmm.
- Ooh, and a hookup

14:09.065 --> 14:10.284
to the new
Black Panther 2 premiere.

14:10.327 --> 14:11.851
- Okay.
- Yeah, I could fuck

14:11.894 --> 14:12.939
with some Black Panther tickets,
too, actually.

14:12.982 --> 14:14.636
- Me, too.
- Black Panther tickets.

14:14.679 --> 14:16.029
- Black Panther? The...?
- Yeah. The second film.

14:16.072 --> 14:17.508
- Make sure it's
the second film, though.
- Right.

14:17.552 --> 14:18.901
- Right.
- Hey, hold-- hold up.

14:18.945 --> 14:21.382
H-Hold the fuck...

14:21.425 --> 14:22.862
How does any of that, man,

14:22.905 --> 14:25.734
how does any of that
help Black people?

14:25.777 --> 14:28.041
Shit, man, well, look, I'm Black

14:28.084 --> 14:29.999
and it's helping me
a whole, a whole lot, so...

14:33.133 --> 14:36.876
My nigga... are you Black?

14:38.747 --> 14:40.314
Am I...

14:40.357 --> 14:42.882
Am I, am I Black?

14:47.669 --> 14:49.410
Khalil, man,
I don't, I don't even know

14:49.453 --> 14:50.541
what your charity does, man.

14:50.585 --> 14:52.021
It's in my book.

14:52.065 --> 14:53.762
Buy a copy.

14:53.805 --> 14:55.111
It's like Blue Man Group.

14:55.155 --> 14:57.592
But activism.
It's quite genius.

14:57.635 --> 14:59.028
- Al?

14:59.072 --> 15:01.030
- Mm?
- No offense,

15:01.074 --> 15:02.989
but we've been
in social justice awhile.

15:03.032 --> 15:04.555
We know what we're doing.

15:06.166 --> 15:08.124
That's fair. Yep.

15:08.168 --> 15:09.430
I'm just saying
that Black people

15:09.473 --> 15:10.866
don't really fuck with y'all
like that.

15:10.910 --> 15:13.782
I mean, the streets
are saying that-that y'all

15:13.825 --> 15:15.479
- full of shit, so...
- Uh, that's rude.

15:15.523 --> 15:17.568
I mean, come on, man.

15:17.612 --> 15:20.180
Like, we sitting here,
a bunch of Black people--

15:20.223 --> 15:22.269
Black-adjacent influencers--
you know what I'm saying?

15:22.312 --> 15:24.358
Like, I got a lot of ideas.

15:24.401 --> 15:27.361
All right?
I can help you, you know?

15:27.404 --> 15:29.145
If you listen to me, I mean,
you know, just hear me out.

15:31.017 --> 15:33.062
...as soon as I get back,
all right?

15:33.106 --> 15:35.151
It was good to see you.

15:43.638 --> 15:46.597
Hey, um, is there
an Apple Store near here?

15:46.641 --> 15:50.166
- I-I nicked my Watch.
- One moment, sir.

16:22.242 --> 16:22.982
Hi.

16:24.853 --> 16:26.986
Hey. How are you?

16:28.726 --> 16:29.771
Fine.

16:30.859 --> 16:32.643
Good.

16:36.691 --> 16:37.866
What the hell's wrong with you?

16:38.867 --> 16:41.130
What?

16:41.174 --> 16:43.089
Where have you been?

16:43.132 --> 16:45.221
I've been shopping.

16:45.265 --> 16:46.875
I was thinking about
how Grace Jones

16:46.918 --> 16:51.184
has all these, like, male suits,
and I kind of wanted one.

16:51.227 --> 16:53.534
I also got this really cool,
like, '80s wig.

16:54.970 --> 16:56.015
It's been weeks.

16:58.278 --> 17:00.628
You give me a thumbs-up emoji?

17:00.671 --> 17:02.804
Are you serious?

17:02.847 --> 17:05.067
You guys are busy.

17:05.111 --> 17:07.069
You're working.

17:07.113 --> 17:08.592
I'm just kind of
doing my own thing.

17:08.636 --> 17:10.159
It's not really
that big of a deal.

17:10.203 --> 17:12.074
I mean, you guys didn't plan
for me to come here.

17:12.118 --> 17:14.337
Yeah, you can't do that.

17:14.381 --> 17:15.686
Okay? You can't just disappear.

17:15.730 --> 17:17.036
Okay? We're parents.

17:17.079 --> 17:19.081
I mean, what if something
had happened to you?

17:19.125 --> 17:22.302
What if you were,
like, kidnapped?

17:22.345 --> 17:24.260
I called your mom. She didn't
even know where you were.

17:24.304 --> 17:26.871
Does your mom know
where you are right now?

17:26.915 --> 17:29.918
I saw you. I saw what you did.

17:31.006 --> 17:32.616
What?

17:32.660 --> 17:36.664
You stole that from the shop.

17:36.707 --> 17:40.320
This? I just bought this
at Christine's down the street.

17:40.363 --> 17:42.844
You stole it and I am not going
to let you get away with it.

17:42.887 --> 17:45.499
Because I'm Black and you think
I can't pay for it?

17:45.542 --> 17:48.023
- Lady, I think
you've made a mistake.

17:48.067 --> 17:50.634
Call the police. I am holding
you here till the police come.

17:50.678 --> 17:53.724
- Hey. Let go of me.
What is wrong with you?
- Hey. Hey-- What...

17:53.768 --> 17:55.509
- Let go of her.
You're just accusing people.
- Are you crazy?

17:55.552 --> 17:57.380
No, it's all up to me.
You're going to jail.

17:57.424 --> 17:59.121
What-- Get off!

17:59.165 --> 18:00.601
- Is something wrong?
- Yes.

18:00.644 --> 18:03.604
This woman came in
accusing my fiancée

18:03.647 --> 18:05.606
of stealing a wig
that we just bought

18:05.649 --> 18:06.868
- from Christine's.
- She stole it.

18:06.911 --> 18:09.088
Ma'am, are you staying here?

18:09.131 --> 18:11.351
- Uh, I am making
a citizen's arrest.
- Ma'am, leave this hotel

18:11.394 --> 18:13.092
- or I will call the police.

18:21.839 --> 18:23.232
I'm sorry for that, sir.

18:25.582 --> 18:26.888
You know,
they can't find our bags,

18:26.931 --> 18:28.194
they can't find our name
in the system,

18:28.237 --> 18:29.543
they don't know
where our room is.

18:29.586 --> 18:31.936
We're been sitting here
for hours.

18:31.980 --> 18:33.677
She doesn't even like London.

18:33.721 --> 18:35.157
I'm trying
to get her to move here,

18:35.201 --> 18:36.854
and then this racist shit
happens.

18:36.898 --> 18:38.856
- It's-it's unbelievable.
- Let me check on your room.

18:38.900 --> 18:40.206
Regardless, we'll get you
a top room

18:40.249 --> 18:41.990
free of charge for the night.

18:42.033 --> 18:44.384
I can pay for the room.
I just want our bags.

18:44.427 --> 18:46.255
The first night is on us.
Apologies, sir.

18:55.003 --> 18:56.265
Are you staying here?

18:58.615 --> 18:59.790
I am now.

19:03.838 --> 19:05.361
All right, so

19:05.405 --> 19:08.973
we open on a Black girl--
no, a Black woman--

19:09.017 --> 19:10.192
and she is getting paid,
you heard,

19:10.236 --> 19:11.715
'cause she's the boss, right?

19:11.759 --> 19:13.282
So she's only going

19:13.326 --> 19:14.936
to Black businesses
and she's giving her dollars

19:14.979 --> 19:16.938
to the Black businesses,
you know, and one at a time,

19:16.981 --> 19:18.983
just going,
"Hey, reinvest in your hood.

19:19.027 --> 19:20.463
Reinvest in your hood."

19:20.507 --> 19:23.597
And we should just
call that the, um...

19:23.640 --> 19:25.164
Reinvest in Your Hood campaign.

19:27.427 --> 19:29.733
Yeah, I wasn't
listening at first,

19:29.777 --> 19:31.170
but that's actually
not a bad idea.

19:31.213 --> 19:33.737
Yeah, we could do one
for Brixton, too.

19:33.781 --> 19:35.478
- Mm.
- And we can, like,

19:35.522 --> 19:37.915
include their social media
handles or something.

19:37.959 --> 19:39.917
- Mm-hmm.
- Maybe you should think big,

19:39.961 --> 19:42.050
- like scholarships.
- Hey.

19:42.093 --> 19:43.704
- An apprenticeship program
with Black fashion students.
- Yes.

19:43.747 --> 19:45.706
Whoa, whoa, whoa.
Wait a minute, wait a minute.

19:45.749 --> 19:47.055
If I had a sandwich
for every nigga

19:47.098 --> 19:48.752
who thought he could
change something,

19:48.796 --> 19:50.450
- I'd be Jimmy John.
- Yeah.

19:50.493 --> 19:52.930
He's right, y'all. That shit
sounds expensive as hell.

19:55.672 --> 19:57.326
I managed to squeeze out
a discretionary fund

19:57.370 --> 19:58.632
of 60,000 euros.

19:58.675 --> 20:00.416
Damn!

20:00.460 --> 20:03.767
- - 60
- K? Girl, lead with that.

20:03.811 --> 20:05.291
Well, that's a no-brainer.
Why don't we do it

20:05.334 --> 20:07.423
through my organization
Open Arms?

20:07.467 --> 20:10.078
- Mm-hmm.
- Hey, hold up.

20:10.121 --> 20:13.473
You got the
donation money last time, nigga.

20:13.516 --> 20:16.476
- It's my turn.
- That little NAACP
endowment bullshit?

20:16.519 --> 20:17.564
- That don't even count, man.
- Listen, that's not
how it works.

20:17.607 --> 20:19.348
Hey, look, it's time
for Demarco

20:19.392 --> 20:20.219
- to get his.
- Yeah, it don't sound right.

20:20.262 --> 20:21.350
Over my handsome...

20:21.394 --> 20:22.264
That don't sound right
when you say it.

20:22.308 --> 20:23.352
Does he say "nigga" a lot?

20:23.396 --> 20:25.920
- It just don't feel right.
- Decorum!

20:25.963 --> 20:27.748
- Sit down, Dozle.
Why don't you sit down, Dozle?
- I wish you would, Khalil.

20:27.791 --> 20:29.097
- I wish you would, Khalil.
- Sit down, Dozle.

20:29.140 --> 20:30.446
- Why don't you sit...
- Decorum! Decorum.

20:31.926 --> 20:33.884
Sit your asses down.

20:39.150 --> 20:41.892
Eniola, go ahead, baby.

20:42.893 --> 20:45.461
It's Alfred's idea.

20:45.505 --> 20:46.767
He decides.

20:48.508 --> 20:50.249
Hey.

20:50.292 --> 20:52.425
Do the right thing, brother.

20:56.037 --> 20:57.430
Khalil.

20:59.823 --> 21:01.912
I'll hammer out the details
with Marcello.

21:01.956 --> 21:03.523
- Mm-hmm.
- Eniola, can you let Wendy
know I'd like

21:03.566 --> 21:05.481
a five-minute meeting today
if possible?

21:05.525 --> 21:07.483
- Mm-hmm.
- For real? So y'all...

21:07.527 --> 21:08.832
Y'all really gonna do it?

21:08.876 --> 21:11.400
- That's right.
- Ooh, we should get you

21:11.444 --> 21:15.056
to film your own pitch
for Marcello.

21:15.099 --> 21:18.320
Show him how passionate
you are about the campaign.

21:18.364 --> 21:21.149
Yeah. All right.
Yeah, shit. Yeah.

21:21.192 --> 21:23.064
- Yeah, yeah.
- Eniola, can you pack me
a to-go plate?

21:23.107 --> 21:24.326
- I'm not your assistant.
- Meeting adjourned.

21:24.370 --> 21:26.154
- Wow.

21:26.197 --> 21:27.721
- Hey, what's up?
This is Paper Boi,

21:27.764 --> 21:29.853
and I just want to throw
a pitch out there for you.

21:29.897 --> 21:31.855
Uh, you know what I'm saying,
I just got this idea

21:31.899 --> 21:34.249
about Black people making money,
you know what I'm saying,

21:34.293 --> 21:36.251
and putting them Black dollars
in Black hands,

21:36.295 --> 21:38.340
and then we just support
Black businesses, right?

21:38.384 --> 21:39.950
'Cause if you take them dollars
and put them back

21:39.994 --> 21:41.343
in your neighborhood,
your neighborhood will grow.

21:41.387 --> 21:43.040
So I figure we just call it

21:43.084 --> 21:46.870
the Reinvest in Your Hood
campaign, right?

21:46.914 --> 21:48.437
You know what I mean, like,
just, like, think about it.

21:48.481 --> 21:51.048
Reinvest in Your Hood.

21:51.092 --> 21:53.529
Reinvest
in Your Hood.

21:53.573 --> 21:55.749
Reinvest in Your Hood!

22:14.811 --> 22:16.770
Yo! Darius.

22:16.813 --> 22:18.772
Over here.

22:21.340 --> 22:24.386
- How the hell are you?
- Sharon?

22:24.430 --> 22:26.214
One s...
Uh, yeah, brown jollof,

22:26.257 --> 22:27.781
- I'm lost.
- shredded carrots,
golden raisins,

22:27.824 --> 22:29.391
- and kids jollof.
- Um, Eko Chops... What happened?

22:29.435 --> 22:31.480
- Anything else?
- We were just there.

22:31.524 --> 22:34.178
- Sharon. Sharon.
- Yeah, should be ready
in, like, ten minutes.

22:34.222 --> 22:37.181
Yeah, see you then. Bye-bye.

22:37.225 --> 22:39.183
Oh, my God,
I'm so glad to bump into you.

22:39.227 --> 22:41.925
Surprise.

22:41.969 --> 22:45.320
I quit my job
and we bought the place.

22:45.364 --> 22:47.583
You bought the place?

22:47.627 --> 22:50.325
Mm-hmm.
It's a-it's a Naija Bowl now.

22:50.369 --> 22:52.719
Uh, grab a stool.
I'm coming out.

22:52.762 --> 22:54.590
Oh, one Malibu
and one cheesy jollof.

22:54.634 --> 22:57.506
Got it.

23:07.081 --> 23:09.257
Yeah, so the landlord had been
trying to sell for months,

23:09.300 --> 23:11.738
so we just, you know,
sweetened the pot.

23:11.781 --> 23:15.481
So s-she relocated?
Where's Mimi?

23:15.524 --> 23:17.352
I don't know. We actually...

23:17.396 --> 23:19.528
We never exchanged info, so...

23:21.617 --> 23:24.925
Dude, you've got to try this.
I want to get your thoughts.

23:24.968 --> 23:27.275
What's in it?

23:27.318 --> 23:30.060
It's a peach barbecue reduction
and chunks.

23:30.104 --> 23:32.585
I call it The Darius,
'cause you're from Georgia.

23:33.977 --> 23:37.459
Okay. Um...

23:37.503 --> 23:39.026
Don't I gotta pay for this?

23:39.069 --> 23:40.723
No. It's on me.

23:42.769 --> 23:44.510
And your money
is literally no good here.

23:44.553 --> 23:47.077
Card only.

23:47.121 --> 23:48.992
Oh, a customer. BRB.

23:53.997 --> 23:56.304
No. No.

23:56.347 --> 23:57.305
Mm-mmm. Not doing that.

24:02.571 --> 24:04.312
Uh, you should recycle that.

24:08.229 --> 24:09.404
Thank you.

24:16.672 --> 24:18.239
Hey, what's up? It's Paper Boi,

24:18.282 --> 24:19.632
and I just want to throw a
pitch out there for you.

24:19.675 --> 24:22.852
Reinvest in Your Hood.
Your Hood.

24:22.896 --> 24:24.941
Think about it, 'cause if we
take them dollars and put them

24:24.985 --> 24:26.900
back in your neighborhood,
your neighborhood will grow.

24:26.943 --> 24:28.771
Reinvest in Your Hood.

24:28.815 --> 24:30.556
Your Hood. Your Hood.

24:30.599 --> 24:32.296
We're all from some hood, man.

24:32.340 --> 24:33.907
Some hood.

24:33.950 --> 24:35.691
We're all from some hood.

24:35.735 --> 24:38.607
- We're all from some hood.
- Some hood.

24:38.651 --> 24:40.217
We're all from some hood.

24:40.261 --> 24:43.003
Reinvest in Your Hood.

24:43.046 --> 24:45.701
- Reinvest in Your Hood.
- Your hood.

24:45.745 --> 24:47.747
Reinvest in our hoods.

24:47.790 --> 24:49.313
Yeah, see, y'all got
to invest shit.

24:49.357 --> 24:51.533
Talking big money, nigga.

24:51.577 --> 24:54.231
We're all from some hood.

24:54.275 --> 24:55.972
Reinvest in Your Hood.

24:57.583 --> 25:00.368
Reinvest in Your Hood!

25:04.981 --> 25:07.288
Why the fuck can't I go in here?
That's some bullshit!

25:09.508 --> 25:11.031
What the fuck y'all clapping
for, man? What's going on?

25:11.074 --> 25:13.947
Monsieur Paper Boi,
your advertisement was super.

25:13.990 --> 25:15.644
Oh, it's super...
I don't give a shit, nigga.

25:15.688 --> 25:17.516
Y'all stole my shit.
What the fuck?

25:17.559 --> 25:19.648
No, Al, we made the commercial.
You're not happy?

25:19.692 --> 25:21.694
Nigga, you All Lives Matter-ed
my shit.

25:21.737 --> 25:23.870
- Hell no I ain't happy.
- No, it's more inclusive,
uh, like this.

25:23.913 --> 25:25.611
It's m-more attitude
of collaboration.

25:25.654 --> 25:27.874
Hey, look, tell me this,
tell me this.

25:27.917 --> 25:29.658
What y'all do about
the programs in Atlanta, huh?

25:29.702 --> 25:31.399
We farmed it out
to the Red Cross, I believe.

25:31.442 --> 25:32.966
- The Red Cross?!
- Yeah, you know,
like blood drives.

25:33.009 --> 25:34.184
Nigga, I know what the fuck
the Red Cross is!

25:34.228 --> 25:36.273
It's the worst one!

25:36.317 --> 25:38.275
- Everybody needs blood.
- That ain't what
I asked for, man.

25:38.319 --> 25:39.668
Them niggas ain't never gonna
see that fucking money now.

25:39.712 --> 25:41.061
- Alfred, a word. Outside.
- What?! You tell me about

25:41.104 --> 25:42.497
- the fucking Red Cross...
- Outside? Listen, listen.

25:42.541 --> 25:43.846
What the fuck they gonna do
about that shit, man?

25:43.890 --> 25:45.413
And they're supposed to call
it the... You supposed

25:45.456 --> 25:46.588
- to reinvest...
- I need you to...

25:46.632 --> 25:49.243
Get your hands off me!

25:49.286 --> 25:50.897
- Listen, listen, relax.
- I'm talking to you...
Stop playing with me, man!

25:50.940 --> 25:53.029
- Relax, relax.
- What I want to do
is go in there with a bat

25:53.073 --> 25:54.683
- Oh, you want to go in there
and beat their asses...
- and knock they asses...

25:54.727 --> 25:57.425
Yeah, I want to do that, man!
Why you ain't mad?

25:57.468 --> 26:00.776
why?

26:00.820 --> 26:03.213
Why would a company
make a project

26:03.257 --> 26:05.041
that would teach Black people

26:05.085 --> 26:07.522
to stop buying their products
and reinvest in their own?

26:07.566 --> 26:10.090
- Man...
- W-Why would they fund
their own demise?

26:13.136 --> 26:15.269
That's not a business.

26:15.312 --> 26:17.576
That's a charity.

26:17.619 --> 26:19.447
They were never gonna
make that commercial.

26:19.490 --> 26:21.362
- That's why

26:21.405 --> 26:22.885
you need your own nonprofit.

26:24.321 --> 26:26.976
You control that money.

26:27.020 --> 26:29.022
That's how I managed
- to squeeze 100
- K out of them

26:29.065 --> 26:31.677
for my own charity.

26:31.720 --> 26:33.635
Look, I told you,
I've been doing

26:33.679 --> 26:36.377
this social justice thing
a long time.

26:39.598 --> 26:42.775
Hey. Look, Black Panther
premiere is coming up.

26:42.818 --> 26:45.386
Do you want to go?
Got an extra ticket.

26:45.429 --> 26:47.257
No, man.

26:47.301 --> 26:50.173
Whoopi Goldberg and Larenz Tate
are in this one.

26:50.217 --> 26:52.045
Larenz Tate.

26:53.524 --> 26:56.484
- Larenz Tate, hmm?
- Mm-hmm.

26:56.527 --> 26:58.094
No. No, I'm-I'm good. I'm good.

26:58.138 --> 27:00.357
I'm good.

27:00.401 --> 27:02.272
All right, suit yourself.

27:04.579 --> 27:06.363
Think about what I said.

27:14.894 --> 27:17.157
What's up?!

27:32.912 --> 27:35.436
Do you remember on Nickelodeon
around Halloween

27:35.479 --> 27:36.306
they'd have Nick or Treat?

27:37.873 --> 27:40.876
Like "trick or treat"
on-on Nickelodeon?

27:40.920 --> 27:43.096
Oh, yeah, I think I do, yeah.

27:43.139 --> 27:45.446
Think about that.

27:45.489 --> 27:48.231
- Nigga Treat.

27:48.275 --> 27:50.016
- I never heard "Nick or Treat."

27:58.372 --> 28:01.810
I've been playing this song
all over Europe.

28:07.947 --> 28:10.558
You know it?

28:10.601 --> 28:12.821
Yeah, I know this song.

28:12.865 --> 28:15.911
It's pretty.

28:15.955 --> 28:17.913
This surround sound is so good.

28:17.957 --> 28:19.959
Mmm.

28:27.357 --> 28:30.056
I'm sorry about, um...

28:30.099 --> 28:32.493
earlier.

28:33.973 --> 28:36.149
What do you mean?

28:38.194 --> 28:41.676
Before the lady, I...

28:41.720 --> 28:43.156
kind of felt
like I was attacking you.

28:47.203 --> 28:48.944
I was just worried.

28:53.079 --> 28:55.864
Oh, Earn.

28:59.128 --> 29:00.913
You worry about everything.

29:02.131 --> 29:04.786
That's not true.

29:04.830 --> 29:05.961
Yeah, it is.

29:09.704 --> 29:12.838
But you shouldn't be.

29:12.881 --> 29:14.665
You know,

29:14.709 --> 29:17.103
Darius says that...

29:17.146 --> 29:19.845
this is all a simulation.

29:22.630 --> 29:25.633
Yeah, that sounds like him.

29:47.176 --> 29:50.658
Did you, um...

29:50.701 --> 29:52.486
did you steal that wig?
